          "settings": {
            "paragraph_class_name": "richtext-p-section",
            "content": "<p>In Latin and Italian, Musa is the muse, the figure who animates writing, thinking, and creative work. To write in the company of a muse, the ancients believed, was to listen carefully and give shape to what mattered most. It was writing with intention.</p><p>Musa is where I house my writing. It holds my reflections, my newsletter, and in time my books. A space where the clinical, the literary, and the personal meet on the page.</p>"
